---
import AppLayout from '../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
---

<AppLayout title="Current development workflow" description="How the three active sites divide responsibility across GitHub, CircleCI, Vercel, Cloudflare and the local Mac, and why development, CI, Preview, Production and monitoring stay separate." locale="en">
  <div class="shell dev-plan">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-kicker">Development workflow · 2026-09-06</span>
      <h1>How the three active websites are developed now</h1>
      <p class="lede">The goal is not to force every repository onto one vendor. Each layer has one job: GitHub keeps source and history, cloud CI performs acceptance, Preview spends resources only when needed, Production stays simple, and the MacBook remains available for Remote Desktop, SSH and daily work.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="principle-grid" aria-label="Shared principles">
      <article><strong>GitHub = source SSOT</strong><span>Code, configuration, pull requests and auditable history start from GitHub.</span></article>
      <article><strong>CI ≠ deployment</strong><span>A green test run does not mean the website is live, and a successful deployment does not replace testing.</span></article>
      <article><strong>Cloud first, Mac quiet</strong><span>Ordinary CI no longer treats the MacBook as an always-on compute server, and generic CI never falls back to research GPUs.</span></article>
      <article><strong>Exact head + post-merge</strong><span>Validate the current candidate before merge, then validate the version that actually landed on main.</span></article>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Responsibilities by site</h2>
      <div class="site-grid">
        <article class="site-card">
          <div class="eyebrow">BaseModel</div>
          <h3>Research site: heavy acceptance runs in CircleCI</h3>
          <p><strong>Source:</strong> <code>mykcs/basemodel</code></p>
          <p><strong>CI:</strong> CircleCI GitHub App. Deterministic checks and four independent Playwright browser shards run in parallel; the risk planner chooses skip / focused / full.</p>
          <p><strong>Deploy:</strong> Vercel. Preview is reserved for exact heads that need real-page acceptance; main owns Production.</p>
          <p><strong>Fallback:</strong> The Mac/OrbStack runner is manual recovery only and does not auto-start.</p>
          <a href="https://basemodel-preview.vercel.app" rel="noopener">Open Production →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="site-card">
          <div class="eyebrow">fuhuo</div>
          <h3>Static work entrypoint: keep deployment lightweight</h3>
          <p><strong>Source:</strong> <code>mykcs/fuhuo_20260419</code></p>
          <p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> repository-owned machine-profile / remote-policy checks plus the Astro build. It does not gain a second heavy CI system just for account-wide uniformity.</p>
          <p><strong>Deploy:</strong> Vercel Git Integration. Preview build compute is explicit exact-head opt-in; main spends Production build compute only when real site inputs changed.</p>
          <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> Mac/RMC operational scripts are not website deployment inputs; Cloudflare stays non-canonical.</p>
          <a href="https://fuhuo-20260419.vercel.app" rel="noopener">Open Production →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="site-card">
          <div class="eyebrow">mykcs.github.io</div>
          <h3>Personal site: GitHub Pages canonical, Cloudflare for Preview</h3>
          <p><strong>Source:</strong> <code>mykcs/mykcs.github.io</code>, with the Astro app under <code>astro/</code>.</p>
          <p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> <code>pnpm run build</code> is the shared correctness gate; browser / SEO / i18n checks are added when the changed surface requires them.</p>
          <p><strong>Preview:</strong> prefer Wrangler Direct Upload so ordinary development does not consume a Git-connected Cloudflare Pages Build for every commit.</p>
          <p><strong>Production:</strong> GitHub Pages remains canonical; the Cloudflare mirror stays noindex.</p>
          <a href="https://mykcs.github.io/en/" rel="noopener">Open Production →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Flow for an ordinary change</h2>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li><strong>Classify the layer first.</strong><span>Source, CI, Preview, Production and monitoring are separate failure domains.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Finish one coherent branch / PR.</strong><span>Prefer one atomic update instead of repeated provider-triggering micro-commits.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Run the cheapest deterministic gate first.</strong><span>Structure, unit tests and build checks come before the full browser suite.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Escalate browser acceptance by impact.</strong><span>Local changes test locally; shared/global/CI-planner changes fail closed to full.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Create Preview only when a real page must be inspected.</strong><span>Preview is an acceptance tool, not a default side effect of every push.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Verify Production after merge.</strong><span>Main CI, provider deployment status and the public URL are separate acceptance evidence.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="guardrail">
      <h2>What this workflow deliberately avoids</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No 24×7 MacBook CI farm; the Mac prioritizes Remote Desktop Commander, browser work, SSH and daily control.</li>
        <li>No generic CPU CI fallback onto research GPU servers.</li>
        <li>No forcing all three websites onto one provider merely for symmetry.</li>
        <li>No mixing deployment quotas with CI compute quotas, and no treating a monthly free allowance as a permanent fact.</li>
        <li>No weakening final acceptance semantics just to make CI faster; optimization targets trigger timing, impact scope, caching and parallelism.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="note">This is a human-readable projection of the development workflow. Volatile facts such as required checks, provider triggers, Build Watch settings and quotas are owned by current repository configuration and live provider state.</p>
  </div>
</AppLayout>

<style>
  .dev-plan { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  .principle-grid, .site-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 3rem; }
  .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .site-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .principle-grid article, .site-card, .guardrail { border: 1px solid var(--border, #d9d9d9); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface, #fff) 92%, transparent); }
  .principle-grid strong, .principle-grid span { display: block; }
  .principle-grid span { margin-top: .45rem; color: var(--muted, #666); }
  .site-card h3 { margin-top: .4rem; }
  .site-card p { margin: .75rem 0; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted, #666); }
  .flow { display: grid; gap: .85rem; padding-left: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .flow strong, .flow span { display: block; }
  .flow span, .note { color: var(--muted, #666); }
  .guardrail { margin: 2rem 0; }
  .note { max-width: 70ch; font-size: .92rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .site-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
